  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "50a29ed3-d320-472a-b382-174084349d5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 Ridge Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Ridge Regression extends Linear Regression by adding L2 regularization. The regularization term helps reduce the effect of large coefficients and can improve generalization when features are correlated."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 88,
   "id": "cdfb39bf-963e-4cba-b5f9-15d987b20a28",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Ridge Regression\n",
      "MAE  : 16.0335\n",
      "RMSE : 22.1800\n",
      "R²   : 0.5211\n",
      "Time : 0.0355 seconds\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ridge_model = Ridge(alpha=1.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "evaluate_model(\n",
    "    \"Ridge Regression\",\n",
    "    ridge_model,\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    X_test,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    y_test\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e325eb14-da44-4cb6-a8c8-e1286fea6b25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.3 Lasso Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Lasso Regression uses L1 regularization. This can shrink some coefficients toward zero and can therefore perform a form of feature selection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 89,
   "id": "2d477a85-069b-4e85-aa41-314c707fbf1c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Lasso Regression\n",
      "MAE  : 16.0332\n",
      "RMSE : 22.1799\n",
      "R²   : 0.5211\n",
      "Time : 0.0284 seconds\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "lasso_model = Lasso(alpha=0.001, max_iter=10000)\n",
    "\n",
    "evaluate_model(\n",
    "    \"Lasso Regression\",\n",
    "    lasso_model,\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    X_test,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    y_test\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0e030ca5-6321-4164-9388-0a2a20a5c1ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.4 ElasticNet Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "ElasticNet combines L1 and L2 regularization. It provides a compromise between the feature-selection behaviour of Lasso and the coefficient-shrinkage behaviour of Ridge."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 90,
   "id": "a6f15dbf-423c-4128-86fa-bd3c9bc9d868",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "ElasticNet Regression\n",
      "MAE  : 16.0337\n",
      "RMSE : 22.1799\n",
      "R²   : 0.5211\n",
      "Time : 0.0283 seconds\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "elastic_model = ElasticNet(\n",
    "    alpha=0.001,\n",
    "    l1_ratio=0.5,\n",
    "    max_iter=10000\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "evaluate_model(\n",
    "    \"ElasticNet Regression\",\n",
    "    elastic_model,\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    X_test,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    y_test\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "09921f06-b300-41b9-a065-5ff62d408d27",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.5 Polynomial Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Polynomial Regression extends the linear model by adding polynomial combinations of the input features. This allows the model to capture certain nonlinear relationships between the features and house price."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 92,
   "id": "7ae87b37-876c-4587-84f2-f18533191676",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Polynomial Regression\n",
      "MAE  : 19.8143\n",
      "RMSE : 26.6427\n",
      "R²   : 0.3090\n",
      "Time : 0.0529 seconds\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import PolynomialFeatures\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "polynomial_model = Pipeline([\n",
    "    ('poly', PolynomialFeatures(degree=2, include_bias=False)),\n",
    "    ('linear', LinearRegression())\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "evaluate_model(\n",
    "    \"Polynomial Regression\",\n",
    "    polynomial_model,\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    X_test,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    y_test\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0cb7fa0e-cbf8-4a48-9572-62a806738aba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.6 Decision Tree Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Decision Tree Regression predicts the target by recursively splitting the feature space into smaller regions. Unlike linear regression, it can capture nonlinear relationships and interactions between features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 94,
   "id": "195ac981-9f49-4e45-b8e5-29e198ca05b3",
